! Windows: the xlsx gives only the window glass area of each zone (raw_data K: dining 47.17 m2, kitchen 0) and the glazing fraction 0.1711 (Building Summary P7; PDF Table 13: 0.17). The number of windows, their walls (dining zone: east, south and west), the edge margins m1 = 0.6029 m (east and west walls) and m2 = 0.7540 m (south wall) and the top height 1.9817 m are values of the prototype read from its window vertices; they are not in the documents. Only the window height is back-calculated from the xlsx area. The three windows have the same height h (a prototype property, not in the documents), so the total area is A = h x (w_east + w_south + w_west) and h = A / (w_east + w_south + w_west); the widths are w_east = w_west = D_dining - 2 x m1 and w_south = W - 2 x m2, so h = 47.17 / (15.2368 + 21.1007 + 15.2368) = 0.9146 m (the prototype writes 0.91451 m). The swinging door of the kitchen is not in the documents and is removed.
